6484205 #edb/ref 1069 "q-63543" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484205 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484205 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following values of $x$ satisfy the inequality $x-3\\le 11\\,?$\n\nI. $x=18$\n\nII. $x=12$\n\nIII. $x=14$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484205 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "29ea78c3-64d8-500c-9798-23e385fca9d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484205 #edb/ref 1074 "We substitute each value into the given inequality and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $x=18$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & \\le 11 \\\\ 18-3 & \\le 11 \\\\ 15 & \\le 11\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $x=18$ into the inequality leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $x=18$ **does not satisfy** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $x=12$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & \\le 11 \\\\ 12-3 & \\le 11 \\\\ 9 & \\le 11\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $x=12$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $x=12$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $x=14$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & \\le 11 \\\\ 14-3 & \\le 11 \\\\ 11 & \\le 11\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $x=14$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $x=14$ **satisfies** this inequality." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484216 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484216 #edb/ref 1069 "q-63127" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484216 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484216 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following values of $a$ satisfy the inequality $\\frac{a}{2}<10\\,?$\n\nI. $a=10$\n\nII. $a=14$\n\nIII. $a=20$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484216 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "44ec8528-0626-53ff-b6b0-f0595765d80d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484216 #edb/ref 1074 "We substitute each value into the given inequality and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $a=10$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{2} & <10 \\\\ \\frac{10}{2} & <10 \\\\ 5 & <10\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $a=10$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $a=10$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $a=14$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{2} & <10 \\\\ \\frac{14}{2} & <10 \\\\ 7 & <10\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $a=14$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $a=14$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $a=20$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{2} & <10 \\\\ \\frac{20}{2} & <10 \\\\ 10 & <10\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $a=20$ into the inequality leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $a=20$ ** does not satisfy** this inequality." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484221 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484221 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101919" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484221 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484221 #edb/ref 1071 "The value $t=-3$ satisfies which of the following inequalities?\n\nI. $0\\le t-4<7$\n\nII. $t+2>-5$\n\nIII. $\\frac{t}{3}>-3$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484221 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "516935e4-c5da-561b-9d27-f7806d4435cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484221 #edb/ref 1074 "We substitute the given value into each of the inequalities and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $t=-3$ into the first inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\le t-4 & <7 \\\\ 0\\le -3-4 & <7 \\\\ 0\\le -7 & <7\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $t=-3$ leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $t=-3$ ** does not satisfy** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $t=-3$ into the second inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t+2 & >-5 \\\\ -3+2 & >-5 \\\\ -1 & >-5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $t=-3$ leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $t=-3$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $t=-3$ into the third inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{t}{3} & >-3 \\\\ \\frac{-3}{3} & >-3 \\\\ -1 & >-3\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $t=-3$ leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $t=-3$ **satisfies** this inequality." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
